# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git checks files out with CRLF by default. A shell script
# checked out that way fails immediately and obscurely — bash reads the carriage return as part of
# the shebang and reports `/usr/bin/env bash^M: bad interpreter`, or `$'\r': command not found` on
# every line. The file looks perfectly correct in an editor.
*.sh text eol=lf
